#~ msgid ""
#~ "\n"
#~ "## Changelog for 2026.25.2\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "### New\n"
#~ "- **Bookmarks.** You can bookmark the current position of an audio book "
#~ "part, podcast episode or jukebox track, and jump back to it later.\n"
#~ "  - **Adding.** `Ctrl+Win+F12` adds a bookmark from anywhere in Windows, "
#~ "and `F12` does the same inside the Station Browser. A bookmark's default "
#~ "name is its number by position (\"Bookmark 1\", \"Bookmark 2\", and so "
#~ "on).\n"
#~ "  - **Notes.** Each bookmark can carry a text note and/or a recorded "
#~ "voice note.\n"
#~ "  - **Reaching a bookmark.** When playback reaches a bookmark it plays "
#~ "two quick beeps. If the bookmark has a note, playback pauses, NVDA speaks "
#~ "the text and the voice note plays, then playback resumes where it left "
#~ "off.\n"
#~ "  - **Bookmark list.** A list sits next to the Podcasts episode list, the "
#~ "Audio Books library (all parts of the selected book) and the Jukebox "
#~ "tracks list. Press `.` to mark items. The context menu offers play from "
#~ "bookmark, rename, delete selected, add or edit text, add voice note, "
#~ "clear notes, repeat between marked bookmarks and stop repeat.\n"
#~ "  - **Repeat.** \"Repeat Between Marked Bookmarks\" loops the section "
#~ "between the earliest and latest marked bookmark.\n"
#~ "  - **Notes on play.** \"Play from Bookmark\" now speaks the text note "
#~ "and plays the voice note first, then starts playback from that position.\n"
#~ "  - **Audio book rows.** Rows now read \"bookmark name — time — part\", "
#~ "and the book name is no longer repeated.\n"
#~ "  - **Keys on the lists.** `←`, `→`, `Shift+←`, `Shift+→`, `Page Up` and "
#~ "`Page Down` work on the bookmark lists of all three tabs, as on the item "
#~ "lists.\n"
#~ "  - **Clean-up.** The clean-up dialog can delete all bookmarks and their "
#~ "voice notes.\n"
#~ "- **Fine seek (1 second).** `Ctrl+Win+Alt+J` and `Ctrl+Win+Alt+K` rewind "
#~ "or forward by 1 second, for live time-shift and for podcasts, audio books "
#~ "and jukebox tracks. `Alt+←` and `Alt+→` do the same in the Station "
#~ "Browser.\n"
#~ "- **Record every song.** Press `Ctrl+Win+E` three times to keep recording "
#~ "and start a new file at every track change until you stop it.\n"
#~ "  - **Partial songs.** The first and last songs are saved with \"(partial)"
#~ "\" in the name.\n"
#~ "  - **Short pieces.** Pieces shorter than 15 seconds (jingles, flickering "
