#~ "  - **Limits.** It does not work on HLS stations or stations without in-"
#~ "band track titles, and stopping playback does not stop it.\n"
#~ "  - **Double press.** A double press still records the current song, but "
#~ "it now starts about 350 ms after the second press so a third press can "
#~ "change what the sequence means.\n"
#~ "- **Clean-up dialog.** A new **Clean up: reset settings and delete saved "
#~ "data...** button on the settings page lets you reset settings and delete "
#~ "saved data. That covers favourites, podcast subscriptions, audio book "
#~ "libraries, GETEM login, Jukebox list, resume positions, bookmarks, "
#~ "timers, recording plans and more. Nothing is selected by default, and "
#~ "deletion needs a second confirmation. Recordings and liked songs are "
#~ "never touched.\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "### Fixed\n"
#~ "- **Song recordings included the start of the next track.** Recordings "
#~ "now end at the exact point where the station announces a new track. Stop "
#~ "requests take effect immediately, which also helps instant recordings. "
#~ "The old 5-second title polling stays as a fallback for streams without in-"
#~ "band metadata, such as HLS.\n"
#~ "- **Music recognition failed on some stations.**\n"
#~ "  - **HTTP 403 on HLS.** ffmpeg now identifies itself with a VLC User-"
#~ "Agent, and retries with a browser one if the server answers 401 or 403. "
#~ "HLS playlist URLs with query strings are detected correctly.\n"
#~ "  - **SHOUTcast `.nsv` timeouts.** For non-HLS streams, freeAudio records "
#~ "a short sample itself and lets ffmpeg decode that file. It does this up "
#~ "front for `.nsv` URLs and as a fallback whenever the direct read fails.\n"
#~ "  - **Errors.** If both attempts fail, the message shows the reason for "
#~ "each.\n"
#~ "- **Choppy playback of ABC (Australia) HLS stations.** These stations now "
#~ "play through a small local compatibility server that re-wraps the audio "
#~ "in a layout BASS can read. The audio itself is not re-encoded. NVDA "
#~ "announces this once per station per session, and the announcement follows "
#~ "**Mute notifications**.\n"
